===== {"id": "pool4-1", "severity": "minor", "location": "/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/HandlePool.lean:515-516 (contentEnd_noDangling); report /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/reports/fix4-pool.md, section B45", "claim": "Cause: the report leaves out a statement change; this is not a formalization error. The hypothesis swap `(ha : RootHeldConv s)` -> `(h1 : I1 s)` in `contentEnd_noDangling` is not a strengthening on its own: the HEAD statement cannot be derived from the new one. The swap is the same one the kernel fix made in `EndFree.endUse_noDangling`, and fix1-kernel.md says so there (\"the two hypotheses are incomparable\"). fix4-pool.md gives the old and new signatures but never says this. Under `KInv` the new form covers every use, so no caller loses anything.", "evidence": "1) /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/recheck4/incomparable.lean compiles. On the concrete state `sib := deriveEff (deriveEff (S3.init Witness.hst) 0 [1] .modify) 0 [1] .modify` it proves `WF3 sib ∧ NoDangling sib ∧ RootHeldConv sib ∧ ¬ I1 sib` (`#print axioms incomparable`: [propext, Quot.sound]). The old hypotheses therefore hold on a state that the new `I1` hypothesis excludes. 2) /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/recheck4/oldforms.lean compiles. It recovers the NoDangling conclusion from `KInv` alone (`contentEnd_noDangling hk.1 hk.2.1.2.2 hk.2.1.1.1 hpre hw'`). It also re-proves the HEAD forms of `contentEnd_preserves` and `freeSlot_preserves` (KInv ∧ KAux -> KInv' ∧ KAux') from the new pairs, so those two statements are strictly stronger. 3) `#check @xreach_inv` matches HEAD:693-696 exactly. 4) fix1-kernel.md: \"The hypothesis swap `RootHeldConv → I1` in the `*_noDangling` lemmas ... is not a strengthening in isolation: the two hypotheses are incomparable.\" fix4-pool.md lists only the old and new signatures of `contentEnd_noDangling`.", "confirms": 3, "real": true}
===== {"id": "pool4-2", "severity": "minor", "location": "/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/HandlePool.lean:555-556 (contentEnd_preserves docstring) and :1785-1786 (freeSlot_preserves docstring)", "claim": "Cause: docstring wording; no theorem is affected. Both docstrings were rewritten in this diff, and both keep a D.3 quotation that does not match the annex text. The quote leaves out the first subject (\"la correspondance des effets et\") with no ellipsis and changes the verb from plural to singular (\"constitue\" instead of \"constituent\"). The text was already in HEAD and was carried over.", "evidence": "Annex D.3 (/Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.4_pour_validation.md:713): \"la correspondance des effets et la préservation des invariants sous ce droit constituent une **obligation explicite de reconstruction**\". Docstrings at :555-556 and :1786: \"la préservation des invariants sous ce droit constitue une obligation explicite\". The script /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/recheck4/quotes.py flags lines 555 and 1786 as NOT VERBATIM. Among the docstrings this diff changed, these are the only two quotations of the annex that differ from it other than by ellipsis or capitalization.", "confirms": 3, "real": true}
===== {"id": "pool4-3", "severity": "minor", "location": "/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/Lib/HandlePool.lean:700 (xreach_inv docstring)", "claim": "Cause: citation imprecision; this is not a claim beyond what is proved. The diff edited this docstring but kept its first line, which cites the whole conjunction `KInv ∧ KAux` as \"(§57)\". The same diff states three times that `KAux` is not a clause of §57. `xreach_inv` is the only declaration in the formalization that cites `KInv ∧ KAux` as §57.", "evidence": "HandlePool.lean:700: \"`KInv ∧ KAux` (§57) holds on every state reached by kernel steps...\". Module docstring :23-24 (same diff): \"the auxiliary `KAux` (not a clause of §57)\". The new docstrings at :581-582 and :1794-1795 say \"not a clause of §57\". Access/Preserve/Common.lean:13 defines KInv as \"The kernel invariant of §57\", and :15-17 defines `KAux` as an \"Auxiliary invariant carried with `KInv` (§40, §49.7)\". `grep -rn \"KInv ∧ KAux\\` (§57)\" Ern` matches only HandlePool.lean:700. Checks that passed (no finding): `lake build` reports \"Build completed successfully (28 jobs)\", and `lake env lean Ern/Lib/HandlePool.lean` prints nothing. The forbidden-token grep prints nothing. `axcheck.sh Ern.Lib.HandlePool` reports 661 constants, 240 theorems and `#[]`. In the diff with docstrings removed (strip_doc_only.py), the only non-docstring changes are the module `/-! -/` text and the B45 code; B48 changed no code. doccheck.py: 278 `/-- -/` docstrings (255 on declarations, 23 on fields), none without the literal \"HandlePool v0.4 annex\", and no declaration without a docstring. At HEAD the same script finds 42 def/theorem/inductive docstrings without it, which matches B48. No new line exceeds 100 characters.", "confirms": 3, "real": true}
===== {"id": "ds4-1", "severity": "minor", "location": "formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean:658-659 (docstring of rewind_ok_iff)", "claim": "The docstring calls Witness.reading_rewind_right \"a reachable state where only §36 rejects\". That overstates the witness. In d16 the §61.1 check of `split` (`internal` exercisable at `Modify`) also fails. The theorem itself is fine: it is machine-checked, axioms are clean, and it matches DS-v1 plus §36 as DS-R12 records. Accurate wording: every DS-v1 condition for success holds and §36 rejects.", "evidence": "The witness's own statement includes the conjunct `¬ d16.kern.ExercisableAt st9.internal .modify`, and its docstring (:1276-1277) says \"`split` of `internal` alone would reject too (`internal` is not exercisable at `Modify`, §61.1)\". Scratch check (recheck4/ds4/Probe.lean, no error, axioms [propext, Quot.sound]): `example : SplitStep K0 st9.internal [above st9 m0] d16.kern .reject := .reject (by decide)`. `effective d16.kern st9.internal 2 = some .modify` and `d16.kern.Active st9.internal ∧ ¬ MetaRight d16.kern st9.entry` are both decided, so `exercisable` is the failing SplitPre field. readings/datastack.md:141-142 (R3) itself says: \"Not proved here: whether the explicit §36 check ever rejects when the split check of §61.1 ... would accept.\"", "confirms": 2, "real": true}
===== {"id": "ds4-2", "severity": "minor", "location": "scratchpad/ref/readings/datastack.md:108 (DS-R12)", "claim": "DS-R12 says that, on library-reachable states, §36 is \"the only reason outside DS-v1's list\". It does not limit this to existing stacks. `RewindStep.noStack` is a second reject outside DS-v1's list, and it happens on a reachable state. `rewind_ok_iff` assumes `hst : D.stacks[j]? = some st`, so it does not support the unrestricted sentence. R3 (:122) says \"for an existing stack\", but DS-R12 drops that restriction.", "evidence": "DS-v1 (brief.md obligation 6, verbatim): \"rewind m fails on a dead or foreign mark, rejects if an active authority derived from internal covers a cell above m, otherwise returns those cells to available and removes m and every mark above it\". Scratch check (Probe.lean, no error): `example : DReach K0 wst d0 ∧ RewindStep K0 0 m0 d0 .reject ∧ ¬ ∃ D', RewindStep K0 0 m0 d0 (.ok D')`. On the initial state, a mark ⟨0,0,0⟩ that is in no list gets `reject` through `noStack`. Under DS-v1 it is a dead or foreign mark (`fail`). readings/datastack.md:37 (DS-R3) records `noStack` only as \"[draft]\", with no alternative.", "confirms": 3, "real": true}
===== {"id": "ds4-3", "severity": "minor", "location": "scratchpad/ref/readings/datastack.md:102-115 (DS-R12); formal/Ern/Lib/DataStack.lean:110 (AdminRight)", "claim": "DS-R12's example only tests the `MetaRight` conjunct of `AdminRight`. The other conjunct, `s.Active st.internal` (the stack is live), also rejects `rewind` on a reachable state where every DS-v1 condition holds. In that case there is a third verdict that no record mentions: DS-v1's \"fails on a dead ... mark\" can be read to cover a live mark of a dead stack, which gives `fail`. So the possible verdicts are reject (model), ok (DS-R12 alternative) and fail (this reading). DS-R2, DS-R3 and DS-R12 record none of the `fail` reading. Cause: missing coverage in the reading record.", "evidence": "Scratch theorem `d17_facts` (Probe.lean, axioms [propext, Quot.sound]). d17 := ⟨releaseEff d11.kern 4, d11.stacks, d11.fresh⟩: the program releases `internal` 4 after the program's release(5). It proves `DReach K0 wst d17 ∧ d17.stacks[0]? = some st9 ∧ LiveMark 0 st9 m0 ∧ ¬ d17.kern.Active st9.internal ∧ (no active authority derived from 4 covers a cell of above st9 m0) ∧ ¬ AdminRight d17.kern st9 ∧ RewindStep K0 0 m0 d17 .reject` (the `.static` constructor). DS-R12 discusses only \"MetaRight requires Modify exercisable on the stack value\".", "confirms": 2, "real": true}
===== {"id": "ds4-4", "severity": "minor", "location": "scratchpad/ref/blocking-report.md:120, :151, :584", "claim": "The uncommitted diff inserts 250 lines into DataStack.lean after line 458. This makes the DataStack line numbers cited in the blocking report wrong. Row B47 also still says that no success-direction theorem exists. These records need refreshing along with the B47 fix.", "evidence": "Report line 151 cites mark_no_aba (:601), grow_same_base (:634), grow_keeps_prefix_bytes (:724), reading_mark (:942), reading_grow_dst (:971) and reading_newStack (:1005). With the diff applied, `grep -n theorem` puts them at 851, 884, 974, 1192, 1221 and 1255. Line 584 cites \"DataStack.lean:1005\": at HEAD that is `theorem reading_newStack`, and in the working tree that line is now a proof line inside another theorem. Line 120 (B47) says: \"No theorem says that `rewind` is `ok` when the mark is live ...\"; `rewind_ok_iff` now exists at :660.", "confirms": 3, "real": true}
